// "[subject] mills N" ([CR#701.17a]): the DECLARATIVE-SUBJECT mill — that
// player puts the top N cards of their library into their graveyard, as one
// simultaneous group ([CR#603.3b]). The keyword action as DATA: a `Composite`
// whose tag is `Mill(who, n)` and whose body is the batch `MoveGroup` of the
// top N of `who`'s library to their graveyard (clamped to library size,
// [CR#701.17b]). There is no bespoke `Mill` verb; the engine realizes the
// stored group move tagged with the `Mill` cause so "milled this way" reads
// find the cards ([CR#701.17c]).
//
// `who` (Param(0)) rides BOTH the atom and the group selection's `whose`. The
// template renders the subject context-aware ("Target player mills five
// cards."); the count spells its noun via the `card|cards` modifier.
//
// Usage: Mills(It, 5) (the announced player target, Tome Scour) /
// Mills(It, 20) (Jace Beleren).
(
    name: "Mills",
    template: "${0} mills ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    body: Composite(
        Mill(Param(0), Param(1)),
        MoveGroup(
            group: TopOfLibrary(count: Param(1), whose: Param(0)),
            arrangement: AnyOrder,
            to: Graveyard,
        ),
    ),
)
